t"},{"type":"text","text":" loop over the subject"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(or over an operator chain built on it) begins. It first receives the value that is current at that moment,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"then every value sent afterwards, in order; values are buffered for it until it consumes them. Values sent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before it subscribed are not replayed. A consumer that subscribes after completion receives only the completion."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"To subscribe before the consumer’s task runs, make the iterator now and hand it over as an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncIteratorSequence"},{"type":"text","text":". Cancelling a task waiting for the next value ends that consumer’s subscription."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Example","anchor":"Example","type":"heading"},{"code":["let subject = CurrentValueSubject(0)","let subscribed = SingleValueSubject<Void>()","","subject.send(1) \/\/ Becomes the current value; no one is subscribed yet.","","Task {","    for try await value in subject.handleEvents(receiveMakeIterator: { try? subscribed.send() }) {","        print(\"Received value: \\(value)\") \/\/ prints 1, then 2, then 3","    }","}","","try await subscribed.execute()","subject.send(2)","subject.send(3)","subject.send(completion: .finished)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}]}],"references":{"doc://Afluent/Sci":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/Sci","title":"_Concurrency.AsyncSequence","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/CurrentValueSubject/AsyncSequence-Implementations":{"abstract":[],"role":"collectionGroup","url":"\/documentation\/afluent\/currentvaluesubject\/asyncsequence-implementations","type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/CurrentValueSubject\/AsyncS